# pr-1443: [docs] development mode: canonical explanation (base for skills; epic #1440)

## Description

Canonical "what is development mode" explanation — the base document for skills, agents and humans operating the knob (owner-requested 2026-11-10).

Contents:
- One-paragraph definition; why it exists (measured evidence summary from epic #1440);
- Exact semantics per mode (`default` inert-by-design / `plan` protocol with committed snapshot + resume rule / `adaptive` deterministic rule + shadowMode);
- Full config surface incl. the not-yet-implemented `spawn` slice (marked as such);
- Operational notes: resolution+logging, reach (story_development + bug_development via shared `initDevelopmentContext`), factory pass-through (dmtools-agentic-workflows#92), pack-version path (AGENTS_VERSION=latest — no bump), interruption/retry interplay;
- Status table (what landed / queued / postponed) with links.

Placement rationale: engine repo owns the semantics (docs/ already hosts machine-factory-integration.md); workflows-side pass-through record stays in dmtools-agentic-workflows#92. Positioned as base material for skills.

Refs: #1440 #1435 (merged #1441) #1436 #1437 #1438 · dmtools-agentic-workflows#92

